                <pb facs="0132" n="123" sameAs="frus:frus1940v02/pg123"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">340.1115A/841h: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Bullitt</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-06-06">June 6, 1940</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>594. Reference Department’s 583, June 4. Since <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Washington</hi> after departure from Lisbon will proceed another port for
                    embarkation additional American evacuees estimated at 800, aliens additional to
                    those already specifically authorized by Department should not be embarked at
                    Bordeaux. Lisbon reports expects approximately 100 Americans for embarkation
                    there.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
